  "mach:judgement": "Adopt",
  "mach:judgementReason": "The standard Python library for 3D medical image augmentation and preprocessing in deep learning — fills a gap that general-purpose vision libraries (Albumentations, torchvision) do not cover. Domain-specific transforms include MRI bias field and k-space motion artifact simulation. v1.0.2 released April 2026, 2.4k stars, 262 forks, Apache 2.0, peer-reviewed publication in Computer Methods and Programs in Biomedicine (2021). Originally from UCL/KCL, now community-maintained.",
